## Copyleft and weak-copyleft components in the distributed bundle

### soxr (libsoxr) — LGPL-2.1-or-later

Bundled as a native shared library inside the packaged Python engine
(`engine/txtcaster-engine.spec`, `collect_dynamic_libs("soxr")`). Reaches txtCaster
as a dependency of librosa and is used to resample voice-cloning reference
recordings.

- Upstream: https://sourceforge.net/projects/soxr/
- Python binding: https://github.com/dofuuz/python-soxr
- Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later

Obligations for a distributed binary: this notice, and the recipient's right to
relink txtCaster against a modified soxr. txtCaster links soxr dynamically and
does not modify it, so replacing the bundled shared library satisfies the
relinking requirement.

### FFmpeg — LGPL-3.0-or-later

The Windows installer bundles an unmodified LGPL build of FFmpeg 8.1 (`ffmpeg.exe` and
`ffprobe.exe`) as separate executables with their libraries as shared DLLs (`ffmpeg/` beside the application).
txtCaster runs them as child processes to encode and measure MP3 exports and to
condition voice samples; it does not link FFmpeg into its own binary. The build is
`ffmpeg-n8.1.3-9-g29e619e767-win64-lgpl-shared-8.1` from BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds, pinned
by SHA-256 in `scripts/fetch_ffmpeg_windows.sh`, which also refuses a build
configured with `--enable-gpl` or `--enable-nonfree`. BtbN's LGPL variants are
configured with `--enable-version3`, so the binaries are LGPL version 3. The Linux package does not
bundle FFmpeg; it declares the distribution's `ffmpeg` package as a dependency.

- Upstream: https://ffmpeg.org/
- Corresponding source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/29e619e767 (n8.1.3 plus 9 release-branch commits) and the build
  recipe at https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
- Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later. The LGPLv3 text ships as `ffmpeg/LICENSE.txt` and the
  GPLv3 text it supplements as `ffmpeg/COPYING.GPLv3.txt`; `ffmpeg/SOURCE.txt` names
  the corresponding source. This NOTICE ships as `NOTICE` beside the application.

Obligations for a distributed binary: this notice, the licence text, access to the
corresponding source, and the recipient's right to replace the bundled FFmpeg
executable and DLLs with a modified build, which they can do in place.

## Copyleft components NOT in the distributed bundle

### PyMuPDF — AGPL-3.0 — development and benchmark use only

Declared only in the engine's `bench` dependency group (`engine/pyproject.toml`)
as the native reference backend for benchmarks and the native test suite. It is
not a default group and is not packaged into the engine or the installers.
Shipping it would require an AGPL-compatible licence for txtCaster or a
commercial PyMuPDF licence.

- Upstream: https://github.com/pymupdf/PyMuPDF

