## Model weights

One small model is bundled: the English pronunciation fallback that spells words
missing from the pronunciation dictionary (`engine/txtcaster_engine/tts/g2p/weights/`,
about 6 MB). It is Peter Reid's graphemes-to-phonemes model, US and GB variants,
licensed Apache-2.0, pinned by SHA-256 to revisions a5631b28 and d8357d50 of
https://huggingface.co/PeterReid/graphemes_to_phonemes_en_us and
https://huggingface.co/PeterReid/graphemes_to_phonemes_en_gb. The Apache-2.0 text
ships beside it as `weights/LICENSE`.

Every other model is downloaded at the user's request from the URLs in
`catalog/catalog.json`, and each entry carries its SPDX licence and a
`commercial_ok` flag surfaced in the UI. Weight licences are listed in
`docs/TECH_STACK.md` §7.

Every catalog entry's weights are permissively licensed and allow commercial use.

## Generated audio

Narration produced with the Chatterbox cloning engine carries an inaudible
watermark applied by Resemble AI's Perth watermarker (MIT), which
`ChatterboxTTS.generate()` applies unconditionally. This is disclosed in the
cloning UI; see `docs/TECH_STACK.md` §5.3.
